Hi, and thanks for this wonderful plug-in!  I downloaded the plugin today, but I am experiencing the same "Cannot read property name of 'null'" issue that others reported with spatial BGM when teleporting within a map.  I'm not using any saves, so I know it isn't an old save issue in my case.
I took a look at the code and the error is occurring in AudioManager.stopMushBgm while trying to read AudioManager._currentBgm.name.  I am most definitely not a javascript expert, but while I see AudioManager._currentBgm being referenced in a few places in your code, I can't find where you're actually setting it to anything--hence it can't read the property of a null object.
As a workaround for others who are/were having this problem:
the affected code only runs if your sound source is set to "Cross Fade = true" (which is the default).  Setting Cross Fade to false should prevent this crash until there's (hopefully!) a fix.  This might also explain why only some people were seeing the issue--if they had Cross Fade turned off (or maybe it was off by default in an earlier version of the plugin?) it wouldn't crash.
EDIT: Also, just wanted to add that this isn't an issue with teleporting, it's an issue with the BGM automatically stopping because of the teleportation.  I get the same crash if I create a manually triggered event to "Stop All Mush BGMs," too.
EDIT2: I may have found the solution.  The original AudioManager.playBgm method contains the line
this.updateCurrentBgm(bgm,pos)
which sets the _currentBgm object properties, but there's no equivalent in your .
playMushBgm
method.  Including that command eliminates the error for me, even with Cross Fade enabled:
AudioManager.playMushBgm = function(bgm, channel, autoRemover, interrupt, pos) {    
    if (bgm.name) {
        if (this.getBgmFromChannel(channel)) {
            ...
            ...
            this._bgmBuffers.push(buffer);
            buffer.play(true, pos || 0);
            if (!this._meBuffer) {
                buffer.play(true, pos || 0);
                this.updateMushBgmParameters(buffer, bgm);
            }           
        }
        this.updateCurrentBgm(bgm, pos); // <<<<< sets _currentBgm object
    }
};

